{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Research complete.\n\nEvidence: 2026 work supports selective, preservation-aware compression rather than blind shortening. “Valid ≠ Necessary” removed 31–53% of reasoning tokens while preserving accuracy; “When LLMs Over-Answer” reduced redundant answers 37% and non-core text 31%; “The Sleeping Agent” showed that an explicit preservation rule raised date retention from 3.05% to 62.39%; “Context Compression Cost” showed unchanged completion can hide extra state-retrieval work. Published 2025 studies add that uncertainty drives repetition/enumeration, long context hurts even with perfect retrieval, judges favor information mass, and adaptive budgets outperform tiny fixed caps.\n\nOSS convergence: OpenAI and Anthropic require every token to earn its place while protecting load-bearing context; OpenAI and Superpowers use progressive disclosure and cross-references; Anthropic recommends positive concise examples and qualitative rather than hard universal caps; wshobson statically scores exact repetition and imperative density but gives token efficiency only 9% weight; Claude Code scopes findings and uses confidence thresholds.\n\nRecommendation: require the minimum sufficient durable record, artifact-specific schemas, a keep/compress/delete pass, exact-fact preservation, and canonical links. Block only objective defects (substantial exact duplication, unsummarized transcript dumps, structurally empty updates); keep length, near-duplication, filler, paragraph length, alternative sprawl, and imperative density advisory. Evaluate completeness/relevance separately from length and measure downstream state reacquisition. No repository files changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788412934808409001,"uuid":"a58ffa58-ad33-4bf0-a677-e5520fd37019"}